RESIDUE STATE CONTRACT

Each state carries finite real-valued κ and ρ observables.
The massless convergent subset is:
    M₀ = { x ∈ X : κ(x) = 0 and ρ(x) = 0 }.

For a finite cycle C, residue score is the sum of |ρ(L_g(x))| over x ∈ C.
Residue minimization is relative to the candidates evaluated together.
